{
 "note": "Barnard Park Sports Pavilion, Busselton (2017, between Barnard Park West and East ovals, by Geographe Bay Rd), from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and the City's photos. One storey, coastal-cottage style: a long hipped Surfmist Colorbond roof that carries on down over a verandah all the way round on slim charcoal posts, a cross gable in the middle of each long side with pale blue weatherboard in the gable, pale blue weatherboard walls and a lot of glazing to the function room and both ovals. The real roof has small gablets at the north and south ends, drawn here as plain hips. Front = the west side, on the car park road (the east side, to the oval, is the same). Metres: x north to south along the building, y east from the west edge of the verandah.",
